# infra/deploy.env — optional host settings for infra/deploy.sh and
# infra/backup/pg-backup.sh. Copy to infra/deploy.env (gitignored), owned by
# the checkout's owner, mode 600. Read as data by infra/deploy-env.sh, never
# sourced: KEY=value per line, the value literal (no quotes, no $VAR), `#`
# comments. A variable set in the caller's environment wins. Paths must be
# absolute. Unknown or repeated keys are refused. Back this file up together
# with infra/.env.

# Required: the compose project this file belongs to (the default project is
# infra). A deploy or backup of another project from this checkout refuses
# the file instead of taking its settings.
COMPOSE_PROJECT=infra

# The edge in front of web and cms: caddy (the bundled Caddy, the default) or
# traefik (a host Traefik with docker-compose.traefik.yml). deploy.sh refuses
# caddy while containers of the project carry Traefik labels.
#DEPLOY_EDGE=traefik

# Where the images come from: build (from this checkout, the default) or
# registry (the published images of the checkout's release tag; only once
# images are published, docs/INSTALL.md).
#DEPLOY_IMAGE_SOURCE=build

# The pre-deploy backup: infra/backup/pg-backup.sh into SINNLOS_BACKUP_DIR
# (which holds the GPG keyring and .backup-keyid). On a host with its own
# backup service instead, BACKUP_RUN names it; deploy.sh then runs
# `sudo -n "$BACKUP_RUN" --kind predeploy sinnlos` (project infra only).
SINNLOS_BACKUP_DIR=/srv/sinnlos-backup
#BACKUP_RUN=/usr/local/sbin/backup-run
# The .env pg-backup.sh backs up (default: infra/.env next to it), and an
# optional plaintext quick-access copy it refreshes (never creates).
#SINNLOS_ENV_FILE=/home/deploy/sinnlos/infra/.env
#SINNLOS_LOCAL_ENV_BACKUP=/home/deploy/.sinnlos-env-backup/.env

# The smoke check's URL (default: WEB_PUBLIC_URL with Caddy, https://<DOMAIN>
# with Traefik).
#SMOKE_URL=https://intranet.example.com
# live-smoke.sh (the end-to-end check of live updates) signs in as two of your
# accounts, both outside MFA_REQUIRED_ROLES (not admins or editors: the script
# cannot type a second-factor code): SMOKE_EMAIL holds the live stream (best
# the author of a published announcement, e.g. a department head: then the
# check covers the notification as well),
# SMOKE_AUTHOR_EMAIL posts one test comment on an announcement and deletes
# it again. PASSWORDS_FILE holds their passwords, one "email password" line
# each (separated by a space or a tab), mode 600. Without them live-smoke
# does not run, and a deploy is recorded as last-known-good only with
# --record-without-live-smoke. docs/INSTALL.md, section 9.
#SMOKE_EMAIL=smoke-reader@intranet.example.com
#SMOKE_AUTHOR_EMAIL=smoke-author@intranet.example.com
#PASSWORDS_FILE=/home/deploy/.sinnlos-smoke-accounts.txt

# Example: a host Traefik with its own backup service (the owner's host):
#   COMPOSE_PROJECT=infra
#   DEPLOY_EDGE=traefik
#   BACKUP_RUN=/usr/local/sbin/backup-run
#   PASSWORDS_FILE=/home/bigemo/.sinnlos-env-backup/demo-account-passwords.txt
